        "A;;RX;AC", "A;OICIIO;RX;AC",
        "A;;RX;RAC", "A;OICIIO;RX;RAC"
      ],
      "explain": "Windows Resource Protection layout. TrustedInstaller owns the folder and has full control so servicing is the only routine writer. SYSTEM and Administrators get only Modify on the folder itself — they cannot change its permissions or take it apart without first taking ownership — but full control (inherit-only) on things created inside later. Users and both app-container groups may read and execute, so sandboxed apps can load system files. CREATOR OWNER gives whoever creates a new item full control over it."
    },
