      "explain": "Machine-wide application data. Any user may create files and folders here (CI: this folder and subfolders) and, through CREATOR OWNER, fully controls what they created — but cannot change other people's items. Frequent source of privilege escalation: installers that put executables or DLLs here without tightening the ACL leave them replaceable by users."
